            "a": "SIADH-MIMICKING PRESENTATION from undiagnosed SMALL CELL LUNG CANCER (SCLC) — SCLC produces ADH (hormone secretion) causing SIADH-like picture, BUT ALSO produces THROMBOTIC tendency (cancer hypercoagulability) → acute renal infarction or intrarenal thrombosis reducing kidney function + contributing to hyponatremia through reduced free water clearance; ADDITIONALLY: anemia + hematuria from occult malignancy (paraneoplastic syndrome or direct kidney involvement); MANAGEMENT: (1) STAT chest CT (look for lung mass), (2) STAT abdominal imaging (assess kidney size, rule out infarction), (3) Assess hematuria source: renal ultrasound, urine cytology, (4) Malignancy workup: tumor markers, paraneoplastic syndrome panel, (5) If SCLC confirmed: oncology consultation (chemotherapy may improve SIADH control), (6) Reconsider SIADH diagnosis — if cancer-induced, treating cancer is priority"
